 "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou explain one result from TwinRead, a research prototype that classifies a colorectal H&E tissue tile. It is not a diagnostic device. Two model heads, reader A and reader B, each give a class and a confidence from 0 to 1. The fused value is the combined call. Classes: ADI adipose tissue; BACK background; DEB debris; LYM lymphocytes; MUC mucus; MUS smooth muscle; NORM normal colon mucosa; STR cancer-associated stroma; TUM colorectal adenocarcinoma epithelium. A tile is flagged for review when the heads disagree or when the review score is high. Write one short paragraph of about 100 words for a doctor. Say what the tile was called, how confident each head was, whether they agree, and whether a pathologist should look at it and why. Use only the numbers given. Do not give a diagnosis or treatment.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nResult: {\"tile\":\"crc_test_186\",\"fused\":{\"class\":\"MUS\",\"confidence\":0.951},\"reader_A\":{\"class\":\"MUS\",\"confidence\":1.0},\"reader_B\":{\"class\":\"MUS\",\"confidence\":0.986},\"flagged_for_review\":true,\"review_score\":0.447,\"reasons\":[\"review_head\"]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
